# The phone's network link is the USB gadget (usb0-gadget.service). It
# gets its address by DHCP from whatever is on the other end of the
# cable: a host sharing its connection, or a router bridging the port
# into its LAN. The DHCP request carries the hostname. With no DHCP
# server the link still has an IPv6 link-local address.
#
# allow-hotplug, not auto: usb0 is brought up by udev when it appears,
# in the background, so a boot without a cable does not wait for a
# lease.

auto lo
iface lo inet loopback

allow-hotplug usb0
iface usb0 inet dhcp
